<% content_for :title, nil %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "#{Store.name} sells sexual health and wellness products, and publishes the education that explains them. Evidence over euphemism, discretion as standard." %>

<%# --- Hero -----------------------------------------------------------------
    Asymmetric and left-weighted rather than centred. Four text elements at
    most, a headline that fits two lines, and one primary action. %>
<section class="wt-container pt-20 pb-20 md:pt-28 md:pb-28">
  <div class="max-w-[54rem]" data-controller="reveal" data-reveal>
    <h1 class="text-display-lg md:text-display-xl text-ink">
      Sexual wellbeing,<br>taken seriously.
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-8 text-lede text-body max-w-[52ch]">
      Products we can explain, and an education library we cite. No euphemisms,
      no shame, and no guessing.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <%# One primary action, and it is the catalogue: the argument for the shop
          is the shop. The standards page keeps its place one level down. %>
      <%= link_to "Shop the catalogue", shop_path, class: "wt-btn wt-btn--primary" %>
      <%= link_to "Our standards", page_path("standards"), class: "wt-btn wt-btn--secondary" %>
      <%= link_to "Why we exist", page_path("about"), class: "wt-btn wt-btn--quiet" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# --- Positioning ----------------------------------------------------------
    Two columns: a claim on the left, the argument on the right. This layout
    family is used once on the page. %>
<section class="border-t border-line" data-controller="reveal" data-reveal>
  <div class="wt-container py-20 md:py-28 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.4fr)] md:gap-16">
    <h2 class="text-heading md:text-heading-lg text-ink max-w-[18ch]">
      Most of this industry talks to you like a joke.
    </h2>

    <div class="wt-prose">
      <p>
        Open a typical shop in this category and you get black backgrounds, neon
        glow, and product names that are embarrassed by their own subject. The
        information you actually need is buried under the winking.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we started from the other direction. Everything we sell has a
        materials list, care instructions and dimensions. Everything we publish
        has a source. Where a question is medical, we say so and point you at a
        clinician instead of quietly implying a product will fix it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is the whole idea. Treat people as adults, and treat the subject
        the way any other part of health gets treated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# --- Operating principles -------------------------------------------------
    A definition list with hairlines between entries, rather than a row of
    equal cards. Long lists get grouped chunks, not a hairline under every row. %>
<section class="border-t border-line bg-paper-sunk" data-controller="reveal" data-reveal>
  <div class="wt-container py-20 md:py-28">
    <h2 class="text-heading md:text-heading-lg text-ink mb-12 max-w-[24ch]">
      Three things we will not do
    </h2>

    <dl class="grid gap-x-16 gap-y-10 md:grid-cols-2 max-w-[76rem]">
      <div class="border-t border-line pt-6">
        <dt class="text-title text-ink font-display mb-3">We will not invent facts.</dt>
        <dd class="text-body max-w-[46ch]">
          No made up statistics, no borrowed credentials, no studies that do not
          exist. If we cite something, you can follow the link and read it.
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-line pt-6">
        <dt class="text-title text-ink font-display mb-3">We will not make medical claims.</dt>
        <dd class="text-body max-w-[46ch]">
          A product can be described accurately without pretending to be a
          treatment. Anything clinical belongs with a clinician.
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-line pt-6">
        <dt class="text-title text-ink font-display mb-3">We will not sell your privacy.</dt>
        <dd class="text-body max-w-[46ch]">
          Purchase history and browsing in this category reveal health intent.
          No advertising trackers, no session recording, and nothing in a URL
          that identifies you.
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-line pt-6">
        <dt class="text-title text-ink font-display mb-3">We will not pretend to be discreet.</dt>
        <dd class="text-body max-w-[46ch]">
          Plain packaging and a neutral billing descriptor, stated once, on the
          shipping page. It is a standard we meet, not a slogan we shout.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<%# --- Where to go next -----------------------------------------------------
    A single row of three text links, not cards. Different from every layout
    above it. %>
<section class="border-t border-line" data-controller="reveal" data-reveal>
  <div class="wt-container py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 class="text-heading text-ink mb-8">Start here</h2>

    <ul class="divide-y divide-line border-t border-line">
      <li>
        <%= link_to page_path("standards"), class: "group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 py-6 no-underline" do %>
          <span class="text-title text-ink group-hover:text-accent">How we choose what we stock</span>
          <span class="text-ui text-muted">Standards</span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
      <li>
        <%= link_to page_path("discreet-shipping"), class: "group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 py-6 no-underline" do %>
          <span class="text-title text-ink group-hover:text-accent">What arrives, and what it says on it</span>
          <span class="text-ui text-muted">Shipping</span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
      <li>
        <%= link_to page_path("privacy"), class: "group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 py-6 no-underline" do %>
          <span class="text-title text-ink group-hover:text-accent">What we collect, and what we refuse to</span>
          <span class="text-ui text-muted">Privacy</span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
